1
00:01:00,291 --> 00:01:04,500
AS OF THIS WEEK,
NINE WORKERS HAVE REPORTEDLY DIED.

2
00:01:06,958 --> 00:01:08,666
THE FIRST DEATH TOOK PLACE
ON FEBRUARY 12, 2025

3
00:01:09,708 --> 00:01:11,207
ON THE EDGE OF NEHEA FOREST...

4
00:01:11,208 --> 00:01:12,791
BY THE MINISTRY OF ENVIRONMENT...

5
00:01:15,291 --> 00:01:16,290
How's it going?

6
00:01:16,291 --> 00:01:17,333
You gonna be long?

7
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:20,624
Just two more sentences.
Then I'll send it to Mr. Endy, sir.

8
00:01:20,625 --> 00:01:23,082
I told the printer guy to wait.

9
00:01:23,083 --> 00:01:27,415
But his wife started having the baby.
He had to rush to the hospital.

10
00:01:27,416 --> 00:01:28,999
THE NATIVES REPORTED THE CASE
TO THE HUMAN RIGHTS COMMISSION

11
00:01:29,000 --> 00:01:32,582
If we had ads, I could fill the space.
But we haven't had ads in a long time.

12
00:01:32,583 --> 00:01:33,874
"THIS FOREST ISN'T JUST TREES,
IT'S OUR HOME."

13
00:01:33,875 --> 00:01:36,958
If your article doesn't come in,
we'll have a blank spot.

14
00:01:41,833 --> 00:01:42,958
Done.

15
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,375
I just need to wait
for Mr. Endy's approval.

16
00:01:47,666 --> 00:01:49,957
I made sure that
there won't be any revisions.

17
00:01:49,958 --> 00:01:51,082
It should go straight to print.

18
00:01:51,083 --> 00:01:53,165
Of course you had to be careful.

19
00:01:53,166 --> 00:01:55,582
You're writing about a big company.

20
00:01:55,583 --> 00:01:57,707
Their investors are government officials.

21
00:01:57,708 --> 00:01:59,332
This will make headlines.

22
00:01:59,333 --> 00:02:02,541
They illegally dug up 10,000 hectares
of protected forest for a nickel mine.

23
00:02:03,125 --> 00:02:04,499
No one dares to speak up.

24
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:06,875
Plus, dozens of workers died
under suspicious circumstances.

25
00:02:07,541 --> 00:02:08,416
It's scary, sir.

26
00:02:09,041 --> 00:02:10,499
And you actually went there?

27
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:11,499
Yes, sir.

28
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:15,250
It's a seven-hour drive
from Balikpapan to Nehea Forest.

29
00:02:15,666 --> 00:02:19,291
I've been to Borneo forests before,
but this one was really mysterious.

30
00:02:20,750 --> 00:02:23,624
I can't wait to read your piece.

31
00:02:23,625 --> 00:02:25,207
Best piece I've ever written.

32
00:02:25,208 --> 00:02:26,583
Mr. Endy's going to love it!

33
00:02:27,125 --> 00:02:28,125
That's great!

34
00:02:31,125 --> 00:02:32,124
Hello, sir?

35
00:02:32,125 --> 00:02:34,790
<i>You call this an article?
What are you, an intern?</i>

36
00:02:34,791 --> 00:02:36,124
<i>Get in here, now!</i>

37
00:02:36,125 --> 00:02:37,000
Yes, sir.

38
00:02:38,333 --> 00:02:39,416
Oh no.

39
00:02:41,041 --> 00:02:42,290
I'll be smoking downstairs, Dimas!

40
00:02:42,291 --> 00:02:43,666
Let me know once it's sent to me!

41
00:02:49,291 --> 00:02:50,415
Excuse me, sir.

42
00:02:50,416 --> 00:02:54,250
You went all the way to Borneo,
wasting our money for this?

43
00:02:55,041 --> 00:02:57,874
Writing about homicide
like those trashy online articles?

44
00:02:57,875 --> 00:02:59,958
You're an economics desk reporter!

45
00:03:00,750 --> 00:03:03,000
The illegal mining part is there, sir.

46
00:03:03,666 --> 00:03:05,707
But the workers' deaths are
more compelling...

47
00:03:05,708 --> 00:03:07,457
Don't you get that we're going
out of business?!

48
00:03:07,458 --> 00:03:11,250
People still read us
because we have substance!

49
00:03:12,875 --> 00:03:14,874
If our stories are no different
from anyone else's,

50
00:03:14,875 --> 00:03:16,833
why the hell would they subscribe to us?

51
00:03:17,458 --> 00:03:19,582
You've got 20 minutes to revise.

52
00:03:19,583 --> 00:03:24,749
The lede should be, "Illegal Deforestation
of Protected Forest."

53
00:03:24,750 --> 00:03:27,374
"Vice-President's son's company
is involved."

54
00:03:27,375 --> 00:03:28,250
That's it!

55
00:03:29,000 --> 00:03:29,916
Yes, sir.

56
00:03:31,541 --> 00:03:32,416
Idiot!

57
00:03:33,666 --> 00:03:34,875
MY WIFE

58
00:03:36,916 --> 00:03:37,750
Hello?

59
00:03:38,583 --> 00:03:42,208
<i>You know the editor can handle it.
It doesn't have to be you.</i>

60
00:03:43,208 --> 00:03:45,499
I just fired my editor today.

61
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:46,791
I can't afford to pay them!

62
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:50,458
<i>If the company can't be saved,
then come home.</i>

63
00:03:50,958 --> 00:03:52,915
<i>Save your marriage!</i>

64
00:03:52,916 --> 00:03:56,999
I built this paper from nothing!
Before I met you!

65
00:03:57,000 --> 00:03:59,708
This paper means a lot more
than our marriage!

66
00:04:00,958 --> 00:04:02,375
<i>Fine. Bye.</i>

67
00:04:04,291 --> 00:04:05,625
Fuck!

68
00:05:08,333 --> 00:05:09,125
Dimas!

69
00:05:10,583 --> 00:05:11,541
Mr. Vijay...

70
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:12,791
Help...

71
00:05:34,583 --> 00:05:36,500
MAINTAIN ORDER

72
00:05:43,333 --> 00:05:44,915
Good morning!

73
00:05:44,916 --> 00:05:47,666
Morning, morning, morning!

74
00:05:48,375 --> 00:05:50,749
Today is the same as yesterday,

75
00:05:50,750 --> 00:05:53,000
{\an8}the same as tomorrow.

76
00:05:53,791 --> 00:05:54,833
As always,

77
00:05:55,375 --> 00:05:59,875
you decide whether your day goes smoothly

78
00:06:00,458 --> 00:06:01,916
or the other way round.

79
00:06:02,375 --> 00:06:04,375
You know the rules.

80
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:08,249
Obey, and you live in peace.

81
00:06:08,250 --> 00:06:11,832
Disobey, and face the consequences.

82
00:06:11,833 --> 00:06:14,833
The only freedom you have here

83
00:06:15,875 --> 00:06:19,541
is choosing how you want
to spend your day.

84
00:06:20,916 --> 00:06:21,999
Understood?

85
00:06:22,000 --> 00:06:24,208
Understood, understood, understood!

86
00:06:24,625 --> 00:06:25,874
Everyone's here?
- Yes, sir!

87
00:06:25,875 --> 00:06:27,624
Yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

88
00:06:27,625 --> 00:06:28,625
One missing!

89
00:06:41,041 --> 00:06:42,374
Get down.

90
00:06:42,375 --> 00:06:43,582
I'm sick, sir.

91
00:06:43,583 --> 00:06:45,708
If I stand, my head spins.

92
00:06:55,791 --> 00:06:57,458
Stand up!

93
00:07:22,791 --> 00:07:23,916
Idiot.

94
00:07:31,125 --> 00:07:32,625
He has no religion!

95
00:07:41,791 --> 00:07:43,000
What did you say?

96
00:07:45,750 --> 00:07:48,832
The next hour and a half is
for religious practice.

97
00:07:48,833 --> 00:07:50,290
He has no religion,

98
00:07:50,291 --> 00:07:52,582
so he can rest and recover.

99
00:07:52,583 --> 00:07:56,165
A third of your time here's for religion.

100
00:07:56,166 --> 00:08:01,749
So if you're not religious,
you get a third of the day off?

101
00:08:01,750 --> 00:08:05,291
Religion doesn't force
sick people to pray.

102
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:12,166
If you think you're smarter than me,

103
00:08:12,833 --> 00:08:14,750
don't fool yourself.

104
00:08:16,291 --> 00:08:20,708
Your brain's tiny compared to mine.

105
00:08:25,625 --> 00:08:27,208
Why so quiet?

106
00:08:29,458 --> 00:08:31,666
Picturing yourself as me?

107
00:08:33,333 --> 00:08:35,416
What would you be doing right now
if you were me?

108
00:08:36,458 --> 00:08:39,333
I definitely wouldn't work in
a shitty place like this.

109
00:08:42,625 --> 00:08:44,750
I work here

110
00:08:45,916 --> 00:08:47,750
because I can!

111
00:08:52,250 --> 00:08:53,208
Come on.

112
00:09:07,083 --> 00:09:08,125
Let him go!

113
00:09:09,208 --> 00:09:09,916
Come on!

114
00:09:10,500 --> 00:09:11,333
Fight back!

115
00:09:17,666 --> 00:09:18,500
Come on now.

116
00:09:19,208 --> 00:09:20,166
Come on!

117
00:09:27,791 --> 00:09:30,208
In here, you're excrement.

118
00:09:33,166 --> 00:09:36,208
So if someone gives a damn, like I do,

119
00:09:37,583 --> 00:09:38,791
just be grateful.

120
00:09:39,958 --> 00:09:41,666
Don't act out.

121
00:09:47,625 --> 00:09:48,875
Believe me!

122
00:09:52,083 --> 00:09:53,416
I'm harsh on you

123
00:09:54,750 --> 00:09:56,833
because that's what you need.

124
00:09:59,541 --> 00:10:02,708
I'm the cure to your diseased hearts.

125
00:10:03,375 --> 00:10:06,791
You're all here
because of your own mistakes.

126
00:10:07,791 --> 00:10:11,082
You have no right to complain.

127
00:10:11,083 --> 00:10:13,958
No right to ask for anything!

128
00:10:14,583 --> 00:10:18,750
Just be quiet and follow the rules.

129
00:10:19,791 --> 00:10:21,291
Now go do your religious activities!

130
00:10:22,541 --> 00:10:24,583
Whether you have a religion or not!

131
00:10:28,708 --> 00:10:29,916
Take him to the cage.

132
00:10:43,875 --> 00:10:47,541
No need to throw it like that.
It won't hurt you to be nice.

133
00:10:48,250 --> 00:10:50,666
What if I spit on it first?

134
00:10:55,750 --> 00:10:58,915
Why did Anggoro pick a fight
with Jefry earlier?

135
00:10:58,916 --> 00:11:00,915
Better than this fucker dying.

136
00:11:00,916 --> 00:11:03,832
I didn't ask Anggoro to help.
He thinks everyone needs his help.

137
00:11:03,833 --> 00:11:06,707
Without him, most of us
wouldn't survive in here.

138
00:11:06,708 --> 00:11:10,540
Not me. I'm doing just fine.
- Fine getting beaten up?

139
00:11:10,541 --> 00:11:11,957
Anggoro's not even a good fighter.

140
00:11:11,958 --> 00:11:13,541
But people respect him.

141
00:11:14,041 --> 00:11:15,707
It's his looks.

142
00:11:15,708 --> 00:11:18,207
If I were tall and handsome like him,
people would respect me too.

143
00:11:18,208 --> 00:11:22,082
Handsome guys get stepped on too.
Anggoro's got a real leader's spirit.

144
00:11:22,083 --> 00:11:23,458
That's what he gets respect for.

145
00:11:24,458 --> 00:11:25,290
You?

146
00:11:25,291 --> 00:11:29,416
You're still alive only because
others think you can actually see ghosts.

147
00:11:31,333 --> 00:11:32,750
You lied about that?!

148
00:11:34,333 --> 00:11:35,708
You trying to get me killed?

149
00:11:36,625 --> 00:11:39,457
Confess, Six.
You don't want to die a sinner.

150
00:11:39,458 --> 00:11:41,000
Right.
- Six.

151
00:11:41,416 --> 00:11:44,000
You really don't have religion?
Where will you go when you die?

152
00:11:44,916 --> 00:11:47,665
Six did a mantra when I was sick,
and I got better.

153
00:11:47,666 --> 00:11:48,666
You lied about that too?

154
00:11:50,041 --> 00:11:50,915
But you got better, right?

155
00:11:50,916 --> 00:11:51,999
Fucker.

156
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:55,332
You're a former professor,
and you buy that nonsense?

157
00:11:55,333 --> 00:11:57,374
You're just fresh meat for the dumb.

158
00:11:57,375 --> 00:11:59,540
But Six has a point, Pendi.

159
00:11:59,541 --> 00:12:02,207
You read books every day,
but you're still dumb like us.

160
00:12:02,208 --> 00:12:06,165
If only you could outsmart Jefry
and show that we have brains too.

161
00:12:06,166 --> 00:12:10,374
I'm sick of hearing him lecture us.

162
00:12:10,375 --> 00:12:11,415
Hey, man.

163
00:12:11,416 --> 00:12:12,749
Where's Anggoro?

164
00:12:12,750 --> 00:12:15,083
He's not here. Go away.

165
00:12:16,375 --> 00:12:20,250
Please help me, man. I'm fucked.
- It's none of our business, go away!

166
00:12:21,500 --> 00:12:23,665
Without Anggoro's help, I'm dead for sure.

167
00:12:23,666 --> 00:12:26,165
He's in the cage. He can't help you!

168
00:12:26,166 --> 00:12:29,875
Anggoro's not here, Syafiq.
Go away.

169
00:12:40,708 --> 00:12:41,625
Fuckers!

170
00:12:42,083 --> 00:12:43,291
You idiots!

171
00:12:47,083 --> 00:12:48,458
Don't you mess with me!

172
00:12:48,958 --> 00:12:50,540
You think you own this place?!

173
00:12:50,541 --> 00:12:55,291
Nothing is free in this world! Fuck you!

174
00:12:56,375 --> 00:12:57,540
Listen to me!

175
00:12:57,541 --> 00:13:02,332
Throwing food away
while people out there starve to death!

176
00:13:02,333 --> 00:13:06,207
You brainless fuckers!

177
00:13:06,208 --> 00:13:08,583
Lick it! Fucking lick it clean!

178
00:13:30,250 --> 00:13:31,541
You've got visitors.

179
00:13:32,708 --> 00:13:33,791
Tell them to go home.

180
00:13:34,875 --> 00:13:36,083
What am I, your servant?

181
00:13:39,916 --> 00:13:41,125
Tell them yourself.

182
00:13:41,916 --> 00:13:43,208
I feel bad just looking at their faces.

183
00:14:18,791 --> 00:14:19,915
Where's your mother?

184
00:14:19,916 --> 00:14:22,124
It's just me and Didi, Dad.

185
00:14:22,125 --> 00:14:24,083
What are you doing here?

186
00:14:24,625 --> 00:14:26,708
We haven't seen each other in two months.

187
00:14:27,625 --> 00:14:29,000
We missed you.

188
00:14:30,875 --> 00:14:32,375
Mom didn't want to come.

189
00:14:33,375 --> 00:14:38,207
Our neighbor dropped us off
on his way to work.

190
00:14:38,208 --> 00:14:42,415
Your mom must've been busy
working hard for you guys.

191
00:14:42,416 --> 00:14:43,457
No, Dad.

192
00:14:43,458 --> 00:14:44,541
She...

193
00:14:45,416 --> 00:14:48,000
We think she's going out
with Mr. Alexander.

194
00:14:48,833 --> 00:14:49,790
Alexander who?

195
00:14:49,791 --> 00:14:52,624
Her coworker at the bakery.

196
00:14:52,625 --> 00:14:55,540
He's been visiting
for the last three months.

197
00:14:55,541 --> 00:14:59,666
At first, Mom kicked him out.
But he kept coming.

198
00:15:00,458 --> 00:15:03,291
And I think she's starting to like him.

199
00:15:03,833 --> 00:15:06,332
We don't want Mom to marry him, Dad.

200
00:15:06,333 --> 00:15:08,290
We don't want a father like him.

201
00:15:08,291 --> 00:15:09,291
Why?

202
00:15:10,041 --> 00:15:11,249
Because...

203
00:15:11,250 --> 00:15:12,583
He...

204
00:15:19,041 --> 00:15:20,208
He's ugly, Dad.

205
00:15:21,458 --> 00:15:23,624
Even with a name like Alexander.

206
00:15:23,625 --> 00:15:26,375
See, I'm Bibin, and I look okay.

207
00:15:28,125 --> 00:15:32,707
Your mom can't remarry.
We're still married.

208
00:15:32,708 --> 00:15:37,749
Mom said you were supposed
to be out last year,

209
00:15:37,750 --> 00:15:42,083
but you kept getting into fights,
so you're still here.

210
00:15:42,958 --> 00:15:43,790
Dad.

211
00:15:43,791 --> 00:15:48,332
Please don't fight anymore, Dad.

212
00:15:48,333 --> 00:15:51,749
Didi here asks everyone he meets,

213
00:15:51,750 --> 00:15:55,250
"Which prison is your dad in?"

214
00:15:56,875 --> 00:15:59,500
He thinks all dads are in prison.

215
00:16:01,125 --> 00:16:04,833
We look at your photo
every night before bed.

216
00:16:05,375 --> 00:16:07,000
So we won't forget your face.

217
00:16:08,041 --> 00:16:09,000
Oh, almost forgot.

218
00:16:12,833 --> 00:16:13,915
What's this?

219
00:16:13,916 --> 00:16:16,583
So you won't forget our faces.

220
00:16:23,375 --> 00:16:24,874
What are you playing with here?

221
00:16:24,875 --> 00:16:26,750
That's clay.

222
00:16:27,333 --> 00:16:28,790
We can make all kinds of shapes.

223
00:16:28,791 --> 00:16:37,374
Teacher said that liking to make shapes
is a sign of intelligence.

224
00:16:37,375 --> 00:16:41,165
You imagine it in your mind first,
then create it with your hands.

225
00:16:41,166 --> 00:16:45,124
She also said that it teaches us
to live with purpose.

226
00:16:45,125 --> 00:16:46,250
She's right.

227
00:16:49,083 --> 00:16:50,708
Time to go home now.

228
00:16:51,458 --> 00:16:52,707
Okay, Dad.

229
00:16:52,708 --> 00:16:54,832
Please don't get into trouble
anymore, Dad.

230
00:16:54,833 --> 00:16:56,083
I'm sorry.

231
00:17:03,500 --> 00:17:05,166
I brought you a banana.

232
00:17:07,333 --> 00:17:10,207
Bye, Dad!

233
00:17:10,208 --> 00:17:11,708
Bye, my sons.

234
00:17:28,041 --> 00:17:32,291
NO SMOKING
WELCOME

235
00:17:44,416 --> 00:17:45,333
Poor man.

236
00:17:46,000 --> 00:17:48,333
Just about to repent and then got killed.

237
00:17:49,250 --> 00:17:50,625
Have a smoke and calm down.

238
00:17:52,416 --> 00:17:53,624
Hey, this is expensive.

239
00:17:53,625 --> 00:17:54,541
It's haram.

240
00:17:56,291 --> 00:17:57,833
He's not allowed.

241
00:17:58,333 --> 00:18:00,750
Why are you all squatting here
like egg yolks?

242
00:18:06,875 --> 00:18:07,875
What?

243
00:18:08,875 --> 00:18:11,415
Someone was looking for you,
asking for protection.

244
00:18:11,416 --> 00:18:12,333
Who?

245
00:18:12,958 --> 00:18:13,915
Syafiq.

246
00:18:13,916 --> 00:18:15,833
Oh, heard he wants to quit dealing.

247
00:18:16,750 --> 00:18:18,625
Promised his sick mother.

248
00:18:19,333 --> 00:18:20,375
Where's he?

249
00:18:21,750 --> 00:18:23,166
He got stabbed to death.

250
00:18:24,541 --> 00:18:25,666
Don't look.

251
00:18:26,375 --> 00:18:27,249
I feel guilty now.

252
00:18:27,250 --> 00:18:31,332
You helped me this morning
and ended up in solitary,

253
00:18:31,333 --> 00:18:32,957
and you couldn't help Syafiq.

254
00:18:32,958 --> 00:18:34,458
It's not your fault.

255
00:18:35,166 --> 00:18:36,666
Who visited you?

256
00:18:37,458 --> 00:18:38,915
My kids.

257
00:18:38,916 --> 00:18:40,083
What did they say?

258
00:18:40,791 --> 00:18:44,790
To make sure I stay out of trouble
so I can get out in seven months.

259
00:18:44,791 --> 00:18:46,000
And what did you tell them?

260
00:18:46,541 --> 00:18:47,375
Nothing.

261
00:18:48,583 --> 00:18:50,457
What's your plan when you get out?

262
00:18:50,458 --> 00:18:51,499
Nothing.

263
00:18:51,500 --> 00:18:53,915
There's no point.

264
00:18:53,916 --> 00:18:58,458
In this fucked up country, hard work
means nothing. You know that.

265
00:18:59,125 --> 00:19:00,416
What about your kids, then?

266
00:19:01,500 --> 00:19:03,083
Better off with their mother.

267
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:07,000
My head.

268
00:19:07,958 --> 00:19:09,624
Still not getting better?

269
00:19:09,625 --> 00:19:11,083
He was so noisy last night.

270
00:19:15,083 --> 00:19:18,541
PRISONER TRANSPORT VEHICLE

271
00:19:46,958 --> 00:19:48,833
WARNING - DO NOT APPROACH
THE SAFETY FENCE

272
00:19:50,208 --> 00:19:51,833
Pretty boy!

273
00:19:52,833 --> 00:19:55,458
Pretty boy!

274
00:19:57,500 --> 00:19:58,458
Hey!

275
00:19:59,791 --> 00:20:01,666
You're mine.

276
00:20:03,125 --> 00:20:04,875
Don't give it to anyone else.

277
00:20:08,458 --> 00:20:10,582
I'm gonna split you wide open.

278
00:20:10,583 --> 00:20:11,707
I'll enter you.

279
00:20:11,708 --> 00:20:13,458
Bang you hard.

280
00:20:17,125 --> 00:20:18,500
Make you feel real good.

281
00:20:24,916 --> 00:20:26,125
Smooth meat!

282
00:20:31,125 --> 00:20:32,791
Hey, let me in on the gossip.

283
00:20:33,166 --> 00:20:34,291
Anggoro...

284
00:20:37,458 --> 00:20:39,333
This time, better stay out of it.

285
00:20:39,875 --> 00:20:40,874
Out of what?

286
00:20:40,875 --> 00:20:43,040
You're the one killing your own guys.

287
00:20:43,041 --> 00:20:45,374
Not my problem. Why would I interfere?

288
00:20:45,375 --> 00:20:46,708
Fuck you.

289
00:20:47,458 --> 00:20:49,500
I'm sick of
your holier-than-thou attitude.

290
00:21:02,708 --> 00:21:03,540
36 YEARS OLD

291
00:21:03,541 --> 00:21:04,458
Next.

292
00:21:05,458 --> 00:21:06,208
Dimas.

293
00:21:07,833 --> 00:21:08,833
Quickly.

294
00:21:09,333 --> 00:21:10,290
Hold it straight.

295
00:21:10,291 --> 00:21:12,415
25 YEARS OLD

296
00:21:12,416 --> 00:21:14,125
Look here.

297
00:21:15,083 --> 00:21:16,041
{\an8}Okay, next!

298
00:21:17,208 --> 00:21:17,915
Next!

299
00:21:17,916 --> 00:21:19,583
Okay, pull up your pants.

300
00:21:26,583 --> 00:21:27,666
Pull up your pants.

301
00:21:32,875 --> 00:21:34,000
Dimas Kurniawan.

302
00:21:35,333 --> 00:21:36,250
Yes, sir?

303
00:21:41,500 --> 00:21:42,750
I didn't ask you to sit.

304
00:21:43,875 --> 00:21:44,791
Strip.

305
00:21:51,916 --> 00:21:54,082
Any illegal items on you?

306
00:21:54,083 --> 00:21:55,165
No, sir.

307
00:21:55,166 --> 00:21:56,082
Any drugs?

308
00:21:56,083 --> 00:21:57,083
No, sir.

309
00:21:58,625 --> 00:21:59,416
Pants off.

310
00:22:02,208 --> 00:22:03,375
Pants off.

311
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:09,958
Look at this.

312
00:22:10,750 --> 00:22:13,208
What's that, Pendi?

313
00:22:16,583 --> 00:22:19,415
So I can talk from a distance,
like the Presidential Guard.

314
00:22:19,416 --> 00:22:22,582
A student gave this to me yesterday.

315
00:22:22,583 --> 00:22:24,290
How are you gonna use that here?

316
00:22:24,291 --> 00:22:27,207
What are you, stupid?
I'll give one to my kid later.

317
00:22:27,208 --> 00:22:31,040
He just needs to come
near the prison to talk to me.

318
00:22:31,041 --> 00:22:32,624
What if you get caught?

319
00:22:32,625 --> 00:22:33,749
I won't!

320
00:22:33,750 --> 00:22:35,457
Hey!
- What do you mean you won't?!

321
00:22:35,458 --> 00:22:37,250
Take the new guy around.

322
00:22:39,041 --> 00:22:40,625
Show him around.

323
00:22:41,541 --> 00:22:42,249
Go.

324
00:22:42,250 --> 00:22:43,415
Go ahead.
- You take him.

325
00:22:43,416 --> 00:22:44,332
Now!

326
00:22:44,333 --> 00:22:46,666
Let's go!
- I need to take a dump.

327
00:22:47,291 --> 00:22:49,040
Good to be old, huh?

328
00:22:49,041 --> 00:22:50,083
Come here!

329
00:22:51,541 --> 00:22:52,665
Hey, man!

330
00:22:52,666 --> 00:22:54,457
What's your name?
- Dimas.

331
00:22:54,458 --> 00:22:55,332
I'm Irfan.

332
00:22:55,333 --> 00:22:56,749
Okay, listen up.

333
00:22:56,750 --> 00:22:59,666
Don't mess up when the guard
questions you, or I'm screwed.

334
00:23:00,541 --> 00:23:02,457
This yard is the Judgement Field.

335
00:23:02,458 --> 00:23:05,374
It feels like the freest spot,
but be careful.

336
00:23:05,375 --> 00:23:07,749
Most inmates gather here.

337
00:23:07,750 --> 00:23:11,874
Whether you survive or die
depends on who you hang with.

338
00:23:11,875 --> 00:23:12,916
Look there.

339
00:23:14,541 --> 00:23:17,624
Terrorism inmates.
Big ones who blew up buildings,

340
00:23:17,625 --> 00:23:20,624
and small ones whose bombs
never even went off.

341
00:23:20,625 --> 00:23:22,165
But see,

342
00:23:22,166 --> 00:23:24,040
terror against other religions?

343
00:23:24,041 --> 00:23:25,999
Sadly, not a crime.

344
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:28,291
We call it majority privilege.

345
00:23:29,541 --> 00:23:31,790
Those in front? Celebrities.

346
00:23:31,791 --> 00:23:34,707
Their arrest made huge headlines.

347
00:23:34,708 --> 00:23:38,749
Journalists went crazy,
pushing aside issues that actually matter.

348
00:23:38,750 --> 00:23:41,415
People say it's a diversion.

349
00:23:41,416 --> 00:23:42,332
Me?

350
00:23:42,333 --> 00:23:45,541
I think Indonesians just care more about
celebrities than their own damn lives.

351
00:23:46,291 --> 00:23:47,791
What did I just say?

352
00:23:51,041 --> 00:23:52,375
What about thugs?

353
00:23:53,041 --> 00:23:54,790
Thugs don't go to prison, brother.

354
00:23:54,791 --> 00:23:56,708
They join community organizations.

355
00:23:59,791 --> 00:24:03,749
Stay away from that one.
That's Rendra Oh's gang.

356
00:24:03,750 --> 00:24:08,208
A drug lord. Been in here five years.
He's running his meth lab in here.

357
00:24:09,166 --> 00:24:11,250
Yeah, he totally looks like a boss.

358
00:24:13,333 --> 00:24:15,208
That's not him.

359
00:24:16,125 --> 00:24:18,125
That's Rendra.

360
00:24:19,833 --> 00:24:21,915
Don't underestimate his looks.

361
00:24:21,916 --> 00:24:23,583
He's not here for drugs.

362
00:24:23,958 --> 00:24:26,791
He stabbed someone in a club
just because he hated the music.

363
00:24:35,041 --> 00:24:37,499
He never got caught making drugs in here?

364
00:24:37,500 --> 00:24:40,374
Every inmate and officer knows.

365
00:24:40,375 --> 00:24:43,958
Come on, you're in Indonesia, not Norway.

366
00:24:45,916 --> 00:24:47,290
What about you?

367
00:24:47,291 --> 00:24:48,499
Which gang?

368
00:24:48,500 --> 00:24:50,000
You met Pendi earlier.

369
00:24:50,541 --> 00:24:51,832
He used to be a university lecturer.

370
00:24:51,833 --> 00:24:57,207
He tried to expose corruption on campus.
Got framed for theft.

371
00:24:57,208 --> 00:24:58,457
Across from him is Wildan.

372
00:24:58,458 --> 00:25:01,999
He's the most devoted out of all of us.
Super diligent.

373
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:03,499
Why's he in here?

374
00:25:03,500 --> 00:25:05,333
Claimed he could
double money with prayers.

375
00:25:05,916 --> 00:25:08,708
The sickly one next to him is Six.

376
00:25:10,083 --> 00:25:10,999
Must've been a sixth kid.

377
00:25:11,000 --> 00:25:12,207
You think you're smart?

378
00:25:12,208 --> 00:25:16,040
His mom really wanted a child, and finally
had one with her sixth husband.

379
00:25:16,041 --> 00:25:18,082
What's he in for?
- He scammed people online.

380
00:25:18,083 --> 00:25:20,749
Made them fall in love,
then ripped them off.

381
00:25:20,750 --> 00:25:22,666
One victim reported him.

382
00:25:23,708 --> 00:25:26,749
Next to him is Anggoro, in for robbery.

383
00:25:26,750 --> 00:25:32,040
His house got seized,
even though he had the certificate.

384
00:25:32,041 --> 00:25:36,082
Turns out, the land mafia
wanted to build a luxury resort there.

385
00:25:36,083 --> 00:25:41,958
Anggoro got pissed off,
robbed the guy, and got caught.

386
00:25:45,208 --> 00:25:46,583
What about you, bro?

387
00:25:47,250 --> 00:25:50,665
We're not bros yet.

388
00:25:50,666 --> 00:25:52,457
I'm in for phone scam.

389
00:25:52,458 --> 00:25:53,707
"Hello, sir?"

390
00:25:53,708 --> 00:25:56,499
"Your son was caught with drugs."

391
00:25:56,500 --> 00:25:59,125
"Do you want to handle it yourself,
or should I?"

392
00:26:00,791 --> 00:26:03,582
So you're a gang of scammers and robbers?

393
00:26:03,583 --> 00:26:04,874
We're not exactly a gang.

394
00:26:04,875 --> 00:26:07,707
But in here, if you're alone,
you'll die faster.

395
00:26:07,708 --> 00:26:09,375
I feel bad for the victims.

396
00:26:11,458 --> 00:26:14,499
You feel bad for the victims?
You think I'm the evil one here?

397
00:26:14,500 --> 00:26:15,916
Let me show you what's evil.

398
00:26:18,250 --> 00:26:19,124
Over there.

399
00:26:19,125 --> 00:26:22,374
Block K. Full of corrupt officials
who love stealing from the people.

400
00:26:22,375 --> 00:26:25,124
Their cells are huge and fancy.
They've got fridges, TVs, AC, and Wi-Fi.

401
00:26:25,125 --> 00:26:28,374
They can even leave whenever they want.

402
00:26:28,375 --> 00:26:30,124
See the guards at the door?

403
00:26:30,125 --> 00:26:32,624
They're inmates paid to protect them.

404
00:26:32,625 --> 00:26:35,790
Block K inmates never set foot
in the Judgment Field. Why?

405
00:26:35,791 --> 00:26:39,125
They go straight to hell.
No need to be judged.

406
00:26:40,541 --> 00:26:41,291
Let's go.

407
00:26:43,250 --> 00:26:45,708
Here's the prayer room.

408
00:26:46,541 --> 00:26:48,999
Huh? Prayer room? Inside a prison?

409
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:50,582
Must be dark and damp.

410
00:26:50,583 --> 00:26:53,457
See for yourself.
It's called Musholla Al Prakasa.

411
00:26:53,458 --> 00:26:56,500
Over here. There.

412
00:26:57,625 --> 00:26:58,624
See?

413
00:26:58,625 --> 00:26:59,832
You get it?

414
00:26:59,833 --> 00:27:02,915
We might live in a dumpster,
but our praying place must be luxurious,

415
00:27:02,916 --> 00:27:05,332
so that we can feel
the prestige of our community.

416
00:27:05,333 --> 00:27:06,165
It's quite empty?

417
00:27:06,166 --> 00:27:07,583
But it's luxurious.

418
00:27:08,125 --> 00:27:09,332
We also have an art room.

419
00:27:09,333 --> 00:27:10,207
Also fancy?

420
00:27:10,208 --> 00:27:13,749
In this country, art is not prioritized.
Not like government buildings.

421
00:27:13,750 --> 00:27:15,874
Or chic selfie spots.

422
00:27:15,875 --> 00:27:17,749
But at least we have one.

423
00:27:17,750 --> 00:27:19,624
Not like that!

424
00:27:19,625 --> 00:27:21,125
Here, watch me.

425
00:27:21,666 --> 00:27:24,207
Before we start dancing,
we have to warm up first.

426
00:27:24,208 --> 00:27:25,458
That's Novilham.

427
00:27:27,208 --> 00:27:28,416
He teaches art class.

428
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:30,915
By the way, which cell did you get?

429
00:27:30,916 --> 00:27:32,249
Block C.

430
00:27:32,250 --> 00:27:33,416
Cell number 31.

431
00:27:35,208 --> 00:27:36,207
Oh, damn.

432
00:27:36,208 --> 00:27:37,208
What?

433
00:27:42,708 --> 00:27:43,791
What's with you?

434
00:27:44,291 --> 00:27:45,624
Just showed the new guy around.

435
00:27:45,625 --> 00:27:47,957
I know, the journalist.

436
00:27:47,958 --> 00:27:49,208
He mutilated his boss.

437
00:27:50,541 --> 00:27:51,874
That kid?
- Yes.

438
00:27:51,875 --> 00:27:52,875
That's what they say.

439
00:27:56,208 --> 00:27:57,665
Hope he survives the night.

440
00:27:57,666 --> 00:27:59,832
Seems like someone's trying
to get him killed.

441
00:27:59,833 --> 00:28:01,415
What cell is he in?

442
00:28:01,416 --> 00:28:02,207
Tokek's cell.

443
00:28:02,208 --> 00:28:06,082
He's definitely fucked.
- Damn.

444
00:28:06,083 --> 00:28:07,416
My head...

445
00:28:08,125 --> 00:28:10,666
I'm gonna chop your head off.
I'm sick of your shit!

446
00:28:12,000 --> 00:28:13,207
Don't be hard on him.

447
00:28:13,208 --> 00:28:15,208
You try sleeping through this!

448
00:28:16,041 --> 00:28:17,250
Every waking hour.

449
00:28:20,625 --> 00:28:23,624
<i>Don't take too long.
Direct order from the boss.</i>

450
00:28:23,625 --> 00:28:25,457
Understood, sir. By tomorrow.

451
00:28:25,458 --> 00:28:28,707
<i>This is a model prison,
so the work's easier.</i>

452
00:28:28,708 --> 00:28:33,916
<i>Handle this right,
and you'll be sitting where I am soon.</i>

453
00:28:34,833 --> 00:28:36,124
<i>Being a deputy minister is nice.</i>

454
00:28:36,125 --> 00:28:41,749
<i>You deal with respectable people,
not those animals in prison.</i>

455
00:28:41,750 --> 00:28:42,707
Yes, sir.

456
00:28:42,708 --> 00:28:46,540
<i>You'll become deputy minister this year,
minister in two years.</i>

457
00:28:46,541 --> 00:28:48,624
No, no. No way, sir.

458
00:28:48,625 --> 00:28:51,000
<i>In five years, I may be working for you.</i>

459
00:28:51,875 --> 00:28:53,540
You joke, sir.

460
00:28:53,541 --> 00:28:54,707
<i>All right, then.</i>

461
00:28:54,708 --> 00:28:57,332
Please send my regards to the boss.
<i>- Will do.</i>

462
00:28:57,333 --> 00:29:00,291
Thank you, sir.

463
00:29:02,750 --> 00:29:03,665
You heard that?

464
00:29:03,666 --> 00:29:05,082
Yes, sir.

465
00:29:05,083 --> 00:29:06,583
I've arranged everything, sir.

466
00:29:07,333 --> 00:29:08,540
Keep it clean.

467
00:29:08,541 --> 00:29:10,999
This one's not like the rest of the scum.

468
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:12,540
If he dies,

469
00:29:12,541 --> 00:29:13,957
it'll make headlines.

470
00:29:13,958 --> 00:29:14,958
Understood, sir.

471
00:29:15,458 --> 00:29:16,500
You're dismissed.

472
00:29:27,666 --> 00:29:29,040
What should we do?

473
00:29:29,041 --> 00:29:31,333
What, you think we can just
ask for a transfer?

474
00:29:37,958 --> 00:29:39,082
I gotta tell you something.

475
00:29:39,083 --> 00:29:39,915
You need to be careful.

476
00:29:39,916 --> 00:29:43,165
You'll be in a cell with Tokek.
Looks like a gecko.

477
00:29:43,166 --> 00:29:45,457
I love geckos, so cute.

478
00:29:45,458 --> 00:29:46,874
Not this one, dumbass.

479
00:29:46,875 --> 00:29:48,957
He's had the cell to himself for years.

480
00:29:48,958 --> 00:29:51,249
Anyone who rooms with him
ends up killed.

481
00:29:51,250 --> 00:29:52,708
He is Rendra's hitman.

482
00:29:53,250 --> 00:29:56,790
It seems someone higher up
wants you dead. Stay sharp.

483
00:29:56,791 --> 00:29:58,499
Once you're in, find a weapon.

484
00:29:58,500 --> 00:30:02,541
If he comes at you,
fight back with everything. Got it?

485
00:30:06,000 --> 00:30:09,499
It's nighttime,
and you all know the rules.

486
00:30:09,500 --> 00:30:14,583
I don't care if you were a thug
or gangster out there.

487
00:30:15,041 --> 00:30:16,083
In here,

488
00:30:17,041 --> 00:30:19,000
you play by my rules.

489
00:30:19,458 --> 00:30:23,375
So shut your mouths and sleep tight!

490
00:30:24,333 --> 00:30:26,624
Get inside your cells!

491
00:30:26,625 --> 00:30:27,541
Now!

492
00:30:43,583 --> 00:30:45,750
Where's Tokek?
- I told him to have a drink first.

493
00:30:46,333 --> 00:30:48,499
He's got a job, you idiot!

494
00:30:48,500 --> 00:30:51,333
If he's drunk,
they'll suspect less, right?

495
00:30:51,916 --> 00:30:53,790
I'm doing you and your boss a favor!

496
00:30:53,791 --> 00:30:56,207
Hey. I don't have a boss.

497
00:30:56,208 --> 00:30:57,250
Watch your mouth.

498
00:30:57,958 --> 00:31:01,083
Remember, you're still nothing
but a doormat.

499
00:31:29,083 --> 00:31:30,666
What do we do? He's gonna die!

500
00:31:38,291 --> 00:31:40,041
Fuck.

501
00:31:54,125 --> 00:31:56,000
Dimas.

502
00:32:01,375 --> 00:32:03,125
You wanna get swollen,

503
00:32:04,500 --> 00:32:06,250
or you wanna get blendered?

504
00:32:13,500 --> 00:32:15,082
You're in my bed.

505
00:32:15,083 --> 00:32:17,166
I can't watch.

506
00:32:19,583 --> 00:32:23,500
Gotta carve you up tonight, pretty boy.

507
00:32:33,333 --> 00:32:36,208
But I'm too drunk.

508
00:32:39,125 --> 00:32:40,833
Tomorrow's fine, yeah?

509
00:32:49,750 --> 00:32:50,833
What's wrong with you?

510
00:32:52,250 --> 00:32:53,250
I saw a rat, sir.

511
00:32:54,000 --> 00:32:55,000
Where?

512
00:32:55,333 --> 00:32:56,125
There.

513
00:32:56,666 --> 00:32:57,791
Don't mess with me.

514
00:33:06,625 --> 00:33:10,375
I can't take this anymore.
I'm better off dead...

515
00:33:11,333 --> 00:33:13,082
Can't you die quietly?

516
00:33:13,083 --> 00:33:15,541
I can't sleep, damn it!

517
00:33:16,208 --> 00:33:18,624
If you don't have religion,
where will you go when you die?

518
00:33:18,625 --> 00:33:19,957
I'll send him to hell myself.

519
00:33:19,958 --> 00:33:20,916
Shut it.

520
00:33:22,125 --> 00:33:23,500
It hurts...

521
00:33:43,041 --> 00:33:44,832
You're not sick anymore?

522
00:33:44,833 --> 00:33:46,250
No, I feel great.

523
00:33:48,833 --> 00:33:52,375
He turned into Jackie Chan?
- Dude's lost his mind.

524
00:33:53,208 --> 00:33:56,000
Man, I feel like an athlete.

525
00:34:02,000 --> 00:34:04,166
Did he take the wrong meds?

526
00:34:26,041 --> 00:34:27,832
What a mess.
- A shower would be nice.

527
00:34:27,833 --> 00:34:30,750
I'll ask for AC later.
- The fan isn't even working.

528
00:34:38,708 --> 00:34:41,458
Vin, come here.
What are you doing over there?

529
00:34:42,291 --> 00:34:44,375
Vin.
- Oh, shit.

530
00:34:45,083 --> 00:34:46,207
Where's Six?

531
00:34:46,208 --> 00:34:49,541
He took a shower earlier
and is exercising now.

532
00:34:54,916 --> 00:34:56,499
The kid's still alive?

533
00:34:56,500 --> 00:34:59,249
Tokek was too drunk
to kill him last night.

534
00:34:59,250 --> 00:35:01,499
But today, it will happen for sure.

535
00:35:01,500 --> 00:35:04,708
Let's pray for him.
- Right.

536
00:35:06,125 --> 00:35:06,999
I'm off first.

537
00:35:07,000 --> 00:35:08,208
Okay.

538
00:35:38,791 --> 00:35:40,750
Pick it up, sweetheart.

539
00:35:44,125 --> 00:35:45,208
Pick it up!

540
00:35:47,666 --> 00:35:49,791
Don't bend over.

541
00:36:16,416 --> 00:36:21,458
Your hands are useless, huh?
Let me just cut them off for you.

542
00:36:38,375 --> 00:36:40,625
So you got yourself a little guard dog.

543
00:37:03,916 --> 00:37:06,707
You've got other creatures
living with you.

544
00:37:06,708 --> 00:37:10,208
Rats, cockroaches, bedbugs.

545
00:37:11,500 --> 00:37:16,333
Make your cell nice and comfy for them.

546
00:37:17,125 --> 00:37:20,207
You're able to be here because
the country is funding it.

547
00:37:20,208 --> 00:37:22,000
Be grateful!

548
00:37:22,500 --> 00:37:26,750
Clean your space until it's spotless!

549
00:37:30,958 --> 00:37:34,791
SHIT

550
00:39:24,583 --> 00:39:26,083
Fuck you!

551
00:39:52,916 --> 00:39:54,583
Fucker!

552
00:39:55,625 --> 00:39:58,041
What do you know about being fucked?

553
00:39:58,875 --> 00:40:02,958
Life has fucked me over so many times!

554
00:40:06,541 --> 00:40:08,541
Wanna feel what I feel?

555
00:40:09,125 --> 00:40:11,166
Come at me!

556
00:40:30,291 --> 00:40:32,125
This fucker.

557
00:40:38,250 --> 00:40:39,541
Fucker!

558
00:42:01,375 --> 00:42:02,833
Fuck! What's with you!

559
00:42:03,208 --> 00:42:04,041
You two!

560
00:42:04,833 --> 00:42:07,250
Why is it always you two?

561
00:42:07,958 --> 00:42:10,083
You think this prison...

562
00:42:15,125 --> 00:42:17,000
What's going on?

563
00:42:44,875 --> 00:42:46,082
Who did it?

564
00:42:46,083 --> 00:42:47,540
We'll sort it out
before the police arrive, sir.

565
00:42:47,541 --> 00:42:49,707
They can't and won't come here.

566
00:42:49,708 --> 00:42:50,707
Are you stupid?

567
00:42:50,708 --> 00:42:53,040
If this hits the headlines, we're screwed.

568
00:42:53,041 --> 00:42:55,832
He was a nobody.
Even his family won't show.

569
00:42:55,833 --> 00:42:57,290
Handle it yourself.
- Yes, sir.

570
00:42:57,291 --> 00:43:01,082
This isn't just about me.
If I go down, you're going down with me.

571
00:43:01,083 --> 00:43:03,999
You're already in too deep. Swim smart.
- Understood, sir.

572
00:43:04,000 --> 00:43:04,832
Find out who...

573
00:43:04,833 --> 00:43:07,207
Everything okay, Mr. Sapto?

574
00:43:07,208 --> 00:43:09,665
Sir! So sorry if we disturbed your rest.

575
00:43:09,666 --> 00:43:10,457
All is good, sir.

576
00:43:10,458 --> 00:43:17,583
We've got all the officers
ensuring your comfort and safety.

577
00:43:19,000 --> 00:43:19,957
Thank goodness.

578
00:43:19,958 --> 00:43:21,457
Yes.

579
00:43:21,458 --> 00:43:24,374
I'm trying to be a model citizen now.

580
00:43:24,375 --> 00:43:25,290
Right.

581
00:43:25,291 --> 00:43:27,665
Not going anywhere.
- I understand.

582
00:43:27,666 --> 00:43:31,124
Just staying in my cell. Safe, right?

583
00:43:31,125 --> 00:43:33,041
Of course, sir.

584
00:43:35,375 --> 00:43:39,874
I'll probably head home next week.

585
00:43:39,875 --> 00:43:42,540
I haven't been home in a week.
My poor wife must miss me.

586
00:43:42,541 --> 00:43:44,290
Wife number...?

587
00:43:44,291 --> 00:43:46,083
The third one, of course.

588
00:43:46,750 --> 00:43:49,457
One and two are already sick of my face.

589
00:43:49,458 --> 00:43:52,665
You're such a funny man, sir.

590
00:43:52,666 --> 00:43:56,915
By the way, did you get my gift
for your boy's birthday?

591
00:43:56,916 --> 00:44:01,582
Oh my God.
I forgot to thank you directly.

592
00:44:01,583 --> 00:44:04,291
Thank you so much, sir.
You really didn't have to.

593
00:44:05,291 --> 00:44:06,665
Not at all.

594
00:44:06,666 --> 00:44:08,624
You did say he wanted a Wubicon.

595
00:44:08,625 --> 00:44:09,999
Correct, sir.

596
00:44:10,000 --> 00:44:14,624
Kids these days have expensive taste.

597
00:44:14,625 --> 00:44:18,249
That's good, not like back
in our day, struggling.

598
00:44:18,250 --> 00:44:20,124
You're right again, sir.

599
00:44:20,125 --> 00:44:22,625
All right, then, I'm off to watch a movie.

600
00:44:23,166 --> 00:44:25,124
Very well, sir.

601
00:44:25,125 --> 00:44:28,790
If anything comes up,
just text me, all right?

602
00:44:28,791 --> 00:44:29,874
Will do.

603
00:44:29,875 --> 00:44:31,707
I'm here whenever you need me.

604
00:44:31,708 --> 00:44:32,999
Have a great shift.

605
00:44:33,000 --> 00:44:34,249
And you have a good rest, sir.

606
00:44:34,250 --> 00:44:35,875
Good night, Mr. Sapto.
- Good night, sir.

607
00:44:39,041 --> 00:44:40,750
Find the culprit now!

608
00:44:43,416 --> 00:44:47,124
What do you mean you saw
Tokek walk into his cell?

609
00:44:47,125 --> 00:44:50,082
I swear it was him. He was real.

610
00:44:50,083 --> 00:44:51,457
Not like some see-through ghost.

611
00:44:51,458 --> 00:44:53,290
Like you know
what a ghost even looks like.

612
00:44:53,291 --> 00:44:54,499
That's what they say, right?

613
00:44:54,500 --> 00:44:58,082
Six, if you keep making things up,
we will beat you up ourselves.

614
00:44:58,083 --> 00:44:59,957
Have you ever seen me this serious?

615
00:44:59,958 --> 00:45:01,500
I don't believe you.

616
00:45:02,708 --> 00:45:03,625
Still...

617
00:45:04,916 --> 00:45:05,999
Hey, what are you doing here?!

618
00:45:06,000 --> 00:45:07,624
Hey, shush!
- What's with you?!

619
00:45:07,625 --> 00:45:09,457
Stay away.
- What's wrong with you?

620
00:45:09,458 --> 00:45:10,790
He can't! He shouldn't be here!

621
00:45:10,791 --> 00:45:11,624
Stay away!

622
00:45:11,625 --> 00:45:13,999
Six! Dimas, stay here.
- No, no, no!

623
00:45:14,000 --> 00:45:16,415
Kindness will do you good.
- You stay there!

624
00:45:16,416 --> 00:45:18,540
Don't stay here! Go!
Please, just listen to me!

625
00:45:18,541 --> 00:45:19,916
If you act like this...

626
00:45:20,708 --> 00:45:22,665
Sit down!
- No, let him leave so Six calms down.

627
00:45:22,666 --> 00:45:24,583
Be quiet!
- Calm down.

628
00:45:26,583 --> 00:45:28,625
What are you doing on that side?
Go over there!

629
00:45:31,708 --> 00:45:32,624
Hey.

630
00:45:32,625 --> 00:45:36,957
Do you think they're suspicious of us?

631
00:45:36,958 --> 00:45:39,124
I mean, we always clashed
with Tokek's gang.

632
00:45:39,125 --> 00:45:43,124
But honestly, we'd be better off
if the police investigated.

633
00:45:43,125 --> 00:45:46,416
But that won't happen.
The officers will handle it themselves.

634
00:45:46,875 --> 00:45:48,832
So now we've got two problems.

635
00:45:48,833 --> 00:45:50,624
First, the prison officers,

636
00:45:50,625 --> 00:45:51,666
Second...

637
00:45:53,583 --> 00:45:57,625
Them. They'll think we did it.

638
00:45:58,208 --> 00:46:00,082
Anggoro's gonna protect us, right?

639
00:46:00,083 --> 00:46:01,666
Allah will protect you.

640
00:46:07,000 --> 00:46:08,207
What's wrong with Anton?

641
00:46:08,208 --> 00:46:11,625
His wife ran off with all their savings.

642
00:46:12,916 --> 00:46:14,457
Wait... you see that?

643
00:46:14,458 --> 00:46:16,082
The red thing around Anton?

644
00:46:16,083 --> 00:46:17,624
What are you talking about?
- That!

645
00:46:17,625 --> 00:46:19,332
Like red smoke!

646
00:46:19,333 --> 00:46:20,915
Stop being creepy, Six!

647
00:46:20,916 --> 00:46:23,040
What?
- Nothing's there!

648
00:46:23,041 --> 00:46:25,915
It looks like smoke!
- What do you mean?

649
00:46:25,916 --> 00:46:27,082
Red smoke on his body.

650
00:46:27,083 --> 00:46:32,541
I'm fine. I said I'm fine!
- Don't make a scene.

651
00:46:33,375 --> 00:46:35,040
Around him.
- Enough.

652
00:46:35,041 --> 00:46:36,040
Stop it.

653
00:46:36,041 --> 00:46:36,958
Shut up!

654
00:46:42,625 --> 00:46:43,708
Food's ready!

655
00:46:44,541 --> 00:46:49,041
Let's eat.

656
00:46:53,291 --> 00:46:54,916
What's going on? What happened?

657
00:47:01,625 --> 00:47:04,000
You all know the situation.

658
00:47:05,458 --> 00:47:07,125
I won't say much.

659
00:47:07,625 --> 00:47:11,082
Talking's not my job.

660
00:47:11,083 --> 00:47:12,915
Yet you never stop talking.

661
00:47:12,916 --> 00:47:16,082
If anyone knows who committed
this horrific crime,

662
00:47:16,083 --> 00:47:17,458
step forward now.

663
00:47:19,833 --> 00:47:20,750
Come.

664
00:47:21,666 --> 00:47:22,915
Quickly.

665
00:47:22,916 --> 00:47:23,957
Sir.

666
00:47:23,958 --> 00:47:25,375
Yes?
- I'm scared, sir.

667
00:47:26,083 --> 00:47:30,708
I saw the body. That death wasn't natural.

668
00:47:31,250 --> 00:47:34,375
Why haven't the police come?

669
00:47:46,375 --> 00:47:50,249
I've been trying to keep you all safe.

670
00:47:50,250 --> 00:47:54,166
But I guess you just want to
make things difficult!

671
00:47:56,750 --> 00:47:57,707
Hey.

672
00:47:57,708 --> 00:47:59,750
Did anyone ask you to help him?

673
00:48:03,291 --> 00:48:04,166
No.

674
00:48:04,708 --> 00:48:06,333
Do I need permission for that?

675
00:48:07,041 --> 00:48:08,290
Where were you this morning?

676
00:48:08,291 --> 00:48:11,083
Where else could I go? I'm a prisoner.

677
00:48:15,958 --> 00:48:18,000
You think this is a joke?

678
00:48:19,958 --> 00:48:23,957
Where were you when Tokek was murdered?

679
00:48:23,958 --> 00:48:25,707
In my cell. I have witnesses.

680
00:48:25,708 --> 00:48:27,416
Who? Your friends?

681
00:48:28,750 --> 00:48:30,540
The CCTV might show something else.

682
00:48:30,541 --> 00:48:32,832
What CCTV? They're all dead.

683
00:48:32,833 --> 00:48:33,958
Exactly.

684
00:48:34,833 --> 00:48:38,833
Which means we can do whatever we want.

685
00:48:39,375 --> 00:48:44,250
Nowadays, anything can be staged.

686
00:48:48,125 --> 00:48:50,000
How much longer are you in for?

687
00:48:51,041 --> 00:48:52,000
Seven months?

688
00:48:53,833 --> 00:48:54,916
Forget it.

689
00:48:55,500 --> 00:49:02,541
A murder case like this
could add another 20 years.

690
00:49:11,666 --> 00:49:13,541
There's no breakfast today.

691
00:49:15,416 --> 00:49:18,625
No lunch.

692
00:49:20,000 --> 00:49:21,375
And no dinner.

693
00:49:22,958 --> 00:49:26,125
If no one's coming forward,

694
00:49:27,583 --> 00:49:31,916
there'll be no food
tomorrow or ever again!

695
00:49:32,666 --> 00:49:35,500
To help you understand
what discipline means,

696
00:49:35,958 --> 00:49:41,624
I'm cutting off

697
00:49:41,625 --> 00:49:47,040
electricity, water,

698
00:49:47,041 --> 00:49:51,875
anything that makes your life easier.

699
00:49:52,541 --> 00:49:56,207
You want to act like animals?

700
00:49:56,208 --> 00:50:00,291
Then you'll be treated like animals!

701
00:50:20,000 --> 00:50:21,665
You piece of shit!
- Stay calm.

702
00:50:21,666 --> 00:50:24,915
We're all screwed because of you.
- Don't take the bait!

703
00:50:24,916 --> 00:50:26,625
Fuck you!

704
00:51:52,208 --> 00:51:53,999
You stupid bitch!

705
00:51:54,000 --> 00:51:58,833
I'll escape and kill you myself, bitch!

706
00:54:14,500 --> 00:54:16,124
Why did you kill your boss?

707
00:54:16,125 --> 00:54:18,250
It wasn't me! I didn't kill my boss!

708
00:54:18,666 --> 00:54:20,374
No need to lie. You're not in a court.

709
00:54:20,375 --> 00:54:21,332
I swear!

710
00:54:21,333 --> 00:54:22,457
Even if I did kill him,

711
00:54:22,458 --> 00:54:25,374
no way I could've lifted
and hung him on the ceiling fan!

712
00:54:25,375 --> 00:54:26,874
Then why were you still found guilty?

713
00:54:26,875 --> 00:54:28,082
This is Indonesia.

714
00:54:28,083 --> 00:54:29,750
You think we're in Norway or something?

715
00:54:30,375 --> 00:54:31,915
Maybe your spirit guardian did it.

716
00:54:31,916 --> 00:54:34,290
What? There's no such thing!

717
00:54:34,291 --> 00:54:36,083
Six, come here.

718
00:54:36,833 --> 00:54:37,582
No.

719
00:54:37,583 --> 00:54:39,375
Get over here and tell us what you saw.

720
00:54:41,000 --> 00:54:45,041
After Tokek died, I saw a figure
that looked like him enter your cell.

721
00:54:45,458 --> 00:54:49,666
And just now, after Anton died,
I saw him walking toward you.

722
00:54:50,375 --> 00:54:53,666
I wasn't even at the scene,
so clearly I didn't do it!

723
00:54:54,250 --> 00:54:55,540
I've always been wimpy.

724
00:54:55,541 --> 00:54:57,957
When I was a baby,
even my cries sounded wimpy.

725
00:54:57,958 --> 00:55:00,000
How does that even sound like?!

726
00:55:11,041 --> 00:55:13,499
Actually, I saw something else too.

727
00:55:13,500 --> 00:55:14,624
What?

728
00:55:14,625 --> 00:55:18,499
Before they died,
I saw a red aura around their heads.

729
00:55:18,500 --> 00:55:19,665
Aura?!

730
00:55:19,666 --> 00:55:22,458
I swear I'll stomp on your neck.
You're still making shit up?

731
00:55:23,833 --> 00:55:25,499
I swear, I'll swear on Allah!

732
00:55:25,500 --> 00:55:26,832
But you don't believe in Allah.

733
00:55:26,833 --> 00:55:28,499
Then I'll swear on anything!

734
00:55:28,500 --> 00:55:32,875
Ever since that terrible headache,
I've been seeing weird things.

735
00:55:33,416 --> 00:55:36,790
Tokek and Anton both had
blood-red auras before they died.

736
00:55:36,791 --> 00:55:39,957
How convenient that you just happened
to see their auras.

737
00:55:39,958 --> 00:55:42,291
Now I can see everyone's aura in the dark.

738
00:55:43,041 --> 00:55:44,416
Can you see mine?

739
00:55:44,916 --> 00:55:46,665
Yes.
- What color?

740
00:55:46,666 --> 00:55:47,583
Grey.

741
00:55:48,250 --> 00:55:49,166
What does it mean?

742
00:55:49,875 --> 00:55:50,624
How would I know?

743
00:55:50,625 --> 00:55:54,082
Then what's the point of you
seeing auras, dumbass?!

744
00:55:54,083 --> 00:55:56,125
Gray aura means confusion.

745
00:55:56,625 --> 00:55:58,790
You're religious.
Why do you believe in such nonsense?

746
00:55:58,791 --> 00:56:06,874
In Islam, though it's not called an aura,
there are verses and hadiths.

747
00:56:06,875 --> 00:56:13,124
"Whoever prays often at night,
their face will shine during the day."

748
00:56:13,125 --> 00:56:15,165
Hadith from Ibn Majah.

749
00:56:15,166 --> 00:56:16,541
Yours is light blue.

750
00:56:17,333 --> 00:56:18,707
Honesty and wisdom.

751
00:56:18,708 --> 00:56:22,082
Go to hell.
- Man, that's totally made up.

752
00:56:22,083 --> 00:56:24,500
No way I'm lying. My aura is honesty.
- It's only good when it's him.

753
00:56:25,416 --> 00:56:27,040
Yours is indigo, but murky.

754
00:56:27,041 --> 00:56:28,583
What color is indigo?

755
00:56:29,333 --> 00:56:30,624
Between blue and purple.

756
00:56:30,625 --> 00:56:33,749
If it's murky, it means
you're unsure, conflicted.

757
00:56:33,750 --> 00:56:35,541
Yeah, I'm conflicted about
whether to slap your face or not.

758
00:56:36,125 --> 00:56:39,166
Yours is green, but also murky.

759
00:56:40,958 --> 00:56:42,166
Apathy.

760
00:56:43,458 --> 00:56:46,290
Then what does blood-red mean,
like Tokek's and Anton's?

761
00:56:46,291 --> 00:56:48,999
Anger. Negative energy.

762
00:56:49,000 --> 00:56:51,499
My boss was angry too,
that night before he died.

763
00:56:51,500 --> 00:56:55,082
He fought with his wife,
and our paper was going bankrupt.

764
00:56:55,083 --> 00:57:00,874
So someone's killing people
who have the most negative energy.

765
00:57:00,875 --> 00:57:01,832
But who?

766
00:57:01,833 --> 00:57:02,707
Or what?

767
00:57:02,708 --> 00:57:03,625
Something.

768
00:57:04,166 --> 00:57:05,457
Only if Six isn't making this up.

769
00:57:05,458 --> 00:57:08,415
I'm not! You think it's fun
to see such things?

770
00:57:08,416 --> 00:57:10,915
Enough. We're safe,
since our auras aren't red, right?

771
00:57:10,916 --> 00:57:12,540
Even though they're kinda murky.

772
00:57:12,541 --> 00:57:13,832
Not really.

773
00:57:13,833 --> 00:57:16,790
Auras can change with your mood.

774
00:57:16,791 --> 00:57:20,082
What if it turns red and murky?
How do we fix it?

775
00:57:20,083 --> 00:57:22,208
By doing good deeds.

776
00:57:23,125 --> 00:57:26,874
Cleaning with sincerity, praying, or art.

777
00:57:26,875 --> 00:57:31,165
Doing art can calm you down.
It keeps your aura safe.

778
00:57:31,166 --> 00:57:32,000
Like what?

779
00:57:32,583 --> 00:57:34,915
Painting, singing, dancing.

780
00:57:34,916 --> 00:57:36,499
I can't paint or sing.

781
00:57:36,500 --> 00:57:37,416
Then dance.

782
00:57:37,958 --> 00:57:38,749
I can't dance either.

783
00:57:38,750 --> 00:57:40,624
Everybody can dance.

784
00:57:40,625 --> 00:57:44,332
Screw you. You used to be the quiet one.
Now you won't shut up.

785
00:57:44,333 --> 00:57:48,249
He's right. It's bullshit.
- Stop fooling around.

786
00:57:48,250 --> 00:57:52,041
Enough.
- Come here and explain it.

787
00:57:52,708 --> 00:57:55,457
How long does it take
to learn to read the Quran?

788
00:57:55,458 --> 00:57:57,457
If you're diligent, 48 hours.

789
00:57:57,458 --> 00:57:59,250
That's fast!
- Only if you're diligent.

790
00:58:01,333 --> 00:58:02,540
Hey, wait!

791
00:58:02,541 --> 00:58:03,915
Wait a minute.

792
00:58:03,916 --> 00:58:06,165
What do you want?
- We want to pray!

793
00:58:06,166 --> 00:58:08,416
Find someplace else. It's full here.

794
00:58:09,916 --> 00:58:13,333
